DESCRIPTION:Solstice Sunrise Run at 7:15 a.m.\n\n•    Sign up by December
  17 (click on "Register" button). \n•    FREE\, limited to 30 people.\n
 •    Meeting Location: Paynetown SRA\, Marina parking area (just past be
 ach)\n\nUsher in the winter solstice with a pre-dawn group run\, ending ju
 st in time to sip hot cocoa while we enjoy the sunrise together! The 3-mil
 e route is on park roads\; participants should be able to comfortably run 
 a 10:30 min/mile pace. Bring a headlamp or small hand-held flashlight.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Paynetown SRA\, Marina parking area
SUMMARY:Solstice Sunrise Run\, Paynetown SRA (Monroe Lake)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/solstice-sunrise-run-paynetown-sr
 a-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Monroe Lake DNR
DTSTAMP:20261128T072929Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54585959043003
DTSTART:20270101T203000Z
DTEND:20270101T213000Z
DESCRIPTION:EARLY Registration (thru Dec. 15) is $15 at bit.ly/monroefirstd
 ay \n\nADVANCE Registration (Dec. 15-30) is $20 at bit.ly/monroefirstday\n
 \nSAME-DAY Registration will be $25 (Jan. 1\, cash / check only)\n\n \n\nC
 heck-In / Same-day Registration: 2:15 p.m. to 3:15 p.m. (Fairfax SRA: Bay 
 View Shelter)\n\nRun / Walk Start Time: 3:30 p.m.\n\n \n\nThis is an untim
 ed\, non-competitive run/walk. Choose from a 3.7-mile\, 2.9-mile\, or 1.3-
 mile course – and don’t forget to tap the bell and ring in the new yea
 r as you cross the finish line!\n\n \n\nThe FIRST 300 to register will get
  the 100% embroidered\, collectible\, event patch!\n\n \n\nAll registratio
 ns include…\n\nA food station with soup\, grilled cheese sandwiches\, ho
 t cocoa\, and a wide variety of snacks.A ticket for the prize drawing\, wh
 ich will have TONS of great prizes!Hundreds of free photos for you to down
 load after the event.A large fire to keep you warm while waiting for the s
 tart and enjoying food after you finish.Special note for leisurely walkers
 : Please be aware that all courses close at 5 p.m. and the food station wi
 ll shut down shortly after that.\n\nDogs are not encouraged but are permit
 ted. They must be on a leash of 6' or less at all times\, and we ask that 
 you begin the run/walk at the back of the group. \n\n \n\nCourse Maps\n•
  LONG COURSE\, 3.7-miles: https://connect.garmin.com/app/course/423098311\
 n• MEDIUM COURSE\, 2.9-miles: https://connect.garmin.com/app/course/4230
 98404\n• SHORT COURSE\, 1.3-miles: https://connect.garmin.com/app/course
 /423098477\n\n \n\nQuestions? Contact the Paynetown Activity Center on Mon
 roe Lake at 812-837-9967 or email Jill Vance at jvance@dnr.IN.gov.\n\nThis
  event is presented by Monroe Lake (an Indiana State Park) and cosponsored
  by the Indiana Trail Running Association. Proceeds support public events\
 , programs\, and interpretation at Monroe Lake.
GEO:39.092423;-86.423753
LOCATION:Monroe Lake\, Fairfax State Recreation Area: Bay View Shelter\, 93
 00 S. Fairfax Road in Bloomington    (ignore the "default" SR 446 address)
SUMMARY:14th Annual First Day Trail Run and Walk\, Fairfax SRA (Monroe Lake
 )
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.in.gov/event/14th-annual-first-day-trail-run-a
 nd-walk-fairfax-sra-monroe-lake
CATEGORIES:Events
END:VEVENT
